@page "/privacy"
<PageTitle>Privacy policy</PageTitle>
<section class="privacy">
    <img class="privacy-mark" src="images/gpstrainer-icon.svg" alt="GPS Trainer" width="72" height="72" />
    <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
    <p>Peak Software Consulting, LLC operates gpsTrainer and this website. We do not rent or sell your personal information.</p>

    <h2>What we collect</h2>
    <p>Creating an account asks for a user name, password, email address, first and last name, phone number, street, city, state, and country, and whether the account is marked male. You can also mark that you want email messages. The site does not keep the password in readable form. The phone app can keep the password on the device so the next launch can sign in.</p>
    <p>The account can store a home location, the latitude and longitude you set on the Account page. Maps open there when a course has no points of its own. That home location is not a continuous trail.</p>
    <p>While you track a ride, the phone records the location trail: latitude, longitude, and time, and the pace and distance computed from that trail. On Android, collection can continue in the background only while a ride is being tracked. Before the ride starts, the staging screen uses location while the app is open to show distance to the start.</p>
    <p>Courses, waypoints, intervals, and rides are stored with your account so this site and the phone can share them.</p>
    <p>gpsTrainer does not connect to Strava and does not store Strava workouts.</p>

    <h2>How it is used</h2>
    <p>The account is how you sign in on this site and on the phone. The home location centers maps. A ride's trail is how the app tells you if you are ahead of or behind your goal, and how this site times interval splits after a ride. A course you enable for download is sent to your phone the next time it synchronizes.</p>
    <p>When you ask the editor to follow roads, the points of that request are sent to OpenRouteService to build the route.</p>
    <p>A published course that an admin has approved can be found by other people. A published ride can be used to show interval times. A ride's location trail is stored with that ride.</p>
    <p>The account form can record that you want email messages. This website does not send product mail. A password reset is kept on the server for one hour. This site does not itself deliver that reset by email.</p>

    <h2>How long it is kept</h2>
    <p>Account details, courses, and ride trails stay until they are deleted. This site does not delete them on a schedule.</p>

    <h2>Deletion</h2>
    <p>While you are signed in, the Account page deletes the account and the courses, waypoints, rides, and location trails stored with it. You can also email <a href="mailto:support@gpsTrainer.com">support@gpsTrainer.com</a> and ask for that deletion.</p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>Questions about this policy: <a href="mailto:support@gpsTrainer.com">support@gpsTrainer.com</a></p>
</section>
